\begin{theorem} \label{ComonadicityGradedModules}
    Let \(R\) be a \(G\)-graded ring and let \(I\) be a finitely generated homogeneous ideal of \(R\).
    Then the functor \(\mcalF^I \colon \mcalD_{\graded{G}}^{\comp{I}}(R) \to \mcalD^{\comp{I}}(R)\) \eqref{ForgetfulCompletionFunctorGradedModules} is comonadic, namely, the comparison functor \eqref{ComparisonFunctorGradedModules}
    \begin{equation*}
        (\mcalF^I)' \colon \mcalD_{\graded{G}}^{\comp{I}}(R) \xrightarrow{\simeq} \coMod_G^{\comp{I}}(R)
