ref_dict.thm:main:
\begin{thm}\label{thm:main}
Consider an algebraic variety $X\subset\K^n\setminus\{0\}$, given by an ideal
$I\subset\K[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item The set of initial parts can be described as a fibration of algebraic sets
\[\Init_\nu(X)=\bigsqcup_{\alpha\in\R}\mathbb{V}(\IN_\alpha(I))\setminus\{0\}.\]
\item There exists a set of critical values $\beta_0<\ldots<\beta_r$ such that, for
$i=0,\ldots,r+1$ the function $\alpha\in(\beta_{i-1},\beta_i)\mapsto\IN_\alpha(I)$ is
constant and gives a homogeneous ideal. The ideals $\IN_{\beta_i}(I)$ are not homogeneous
(we set $\beta_{-1}=-\infty$ and $\beta_{r+1}=+\infty$).
\end{enumerate}
\end{thm}

