Fix an ideal $I$ of $\K[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$. There is a finite set of values
$\beta_0<\ldots<\beta_r$ in $\Gamma$ such that $\forall\alpha\in(\beta_{i},\beta_{i+1})$
the initial ideal $\IN_{\underline{\alpha}}(I)$ is constant and homogeneous.
\end{prop}

