and $\langle w,n_{\Gamma'} \rangle \geq 0$ for $\Gamma' \neq \Gamma$ by Theorem (\ref{Theorem_formula_ker_ITT_intro}) with $n_{\Gamma}$ the inner facet normal to $\Gamma$. The last case in the distinction causes $\Phi_{f \vert{Im \, \kappa_f}}$ to be not injective, which implies in particular that the infinitesimal Torelli theorem (ITT) fails for such hypersurfaces $Y_f$. \leavevmode \\ \\
