This corollary follows easily from above: Namely we construct a $3$-dimensional empty polytope $Q$ with $6$ vertices. $Q$ is the convex span of an empty triangle with vertex $(0,0,0)$ and this triangle dilated by $w$. Then we use a theorem of White on empty $3$-simplices to deduce $|Q \cap M| \geq 7$ under the assumption $\langle w,n_{\Gamma} \rangle \leq -2$, contradiction.
