For fixed $\lambda \vdash k$ and $0 \leq h \leq k$, the coefficients $b_{\lambda,h}^{(r)}$ in the expansion of $\chi^{(n-k,\lambda)}(\sigma_{r})$ in Equation (\ref{expgen}) stabilize as $r\to\infty$, and are equal to $a_{\lambda,h}=f^{\lambda\setminus(1^{h})}$ once $r>h$. \label{limr}
