ref_dict.Def:good:
\begin{Definition}
\label{Def:good}
Let  $\rho $ be a representation of a finitely generated group into $\mathrm{Isom}(X)$.
\begin{enumerate}[(a)]
    \item The representation $\rho$ is said to be \emph{stable} if its conjugation orbit 
$\mathrm{Isom}(X)\cdot\rho$ is closed and its centralizer
$Z(\rho)=\{\sigma\in \mathrm{Isom}(X)\mid \sigma\cdot\rho=\rho\} $
is finite.
   \item The representation $\rho$ is said to be
    \emph{good} if it is stable and  
its centralizer $Z(\rho)$ is trivial.
\end{enumerate}
\end{Definition}

